.TH ARIO_DAEMON 1 "November 2026" "Ario" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ario_daemon \- background download service for Ario
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ario_daemon
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Ario daemon manages aria2, downloads, and scheduled queues.
It normally starts automatically with
.BR ario (1).
It can also be run manually and stopped with Ctrl+C or SIGTERM.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print command-line help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the installed version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-host " ADDRESS"
Listen on a loopback address. Default:
.BR 127.0.0.1 .
Also accepts
.BR localhost .
.TP
.BI \-\-port " PORT"
Listen on the specified port, from 1 to 65535. Default: 47812.
.TP
.B \-\-tui-managed
Allow the TUI to manage daemon shutdown.
.SH FILES
Settings are stored in
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ario/server.toml
or
.I \(ti/.config/ario/server.toml
on Linux, and
.I \(ti/Library/Application Support/ario/server.toml
on macOS.
The file is created on first launch.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ario (1),
.BR aria2c (1)
